---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import ArchitectureDiagram from "../components/ArchitectureDiagram.astro";
import { href } from "../lib/paths";

const layers = [
  {
    name: "Core",
    repos: ["iridium-utils", "iridium-config"],
    body: "Shared building blocks with no runtime dependencies. iridium-utils holds URL, encoding, JSON, header, timing, and address helpers that run in Node and in browsers. iridium-config defines one configuration shape for every Iridium service, validates it, and applies IRIDIUM_* environment overrides.",
  },
  {
    name: "Client",
    repos: ["iridium-proxy", "iridium-inspector"],
    body: "Code that runs in the browser. In iridium-proxy, a service worker uses Scramjet to rewrite a page's requests so they travel through a transport instead of going to the network directly. iridium-inspector is a standalone developer tool built on the core helpers.",
  },
  {
    name: "Transport",
    repos: ["iridium-transport"],
    body: "One small interface, Transport, with a connect() call that returns a readable and writable byte stream. Implementations cover direct TCP and TLS from Node, a Wisp client over WebSocket, and an in-memory pair for tests. Every implementation reports failures with the same error codes.",
  },
  {
    name: "Infrastructure",
    repos: ["iridium-proxy", "iridium-status"],
    body: "The server side. iridium-proxy hosts a Wisp endpoint, serves the client files, and exposes health and readiness paths. Before it opens a connection, an address policy resolves the hostname and refuses private, loopback, link-local, and metadata addresses and blocked ports. iridium-status checks published endpoints on a schedule.",
  },
];

const upstream = [
  {
    name: "Scramjet",
    pkg: "@mercuryworkshop/scramjet",
    license: "MIT",
    url: "https://github.com/MercuryWorkshop/scramjet",
    role: "Request and URL rewriting inside a service worker.",
  },
  {
    name: "wisp-js",
    pkg: "@mercuryworkshop/wisp-js",
    license: "LGPL-3.0-or-later",
    url: "https://github.com/MercuryWorkshop/wisp-js",
    role: "Server-side Wisp implementation used by iridium-proxy.",
  },
  {
    name: "epoxy-transport",
    pkg: "@mercuryworkshop/epoxy-transport",
    license: "AGPL-3.0-only",
    url: "https://github.com/MercuryWorkshop/epoxy-transport",
    role: "Browser transport that speaks Wisp and handles TLS in the client.",
  },
];
---

<Base
  title="Infrastructure"
  description="How Iridium's core, client, transport, and infrastructure layers fit together, and the Wisp-based approach to browser networking."
  current={href("/infrastructure/")}
>
  <header class="page-head">
    <div class="ir-container">
      <p class="ir-eyebrow">Infrastructure</p>
      <h1>Four layers, each with one job.</h1>
      <p>
        Open web infrastructure for browser-based networking and proxy applications. The pieces are
        separate repositories so they can be tested, replaced, and reasoned about one at a time.
      </p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="layers-title">
    <div class="ir-container">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2 id="layers-title">Layers</h2>
        <p>From shared helpers up to the server that opens connections.</p>
      </div>
      <ol class="layers">
        {layers.map((layer) => (
          <li>
            <h3>{layer.name}</h3>
            <div>
              <p>{layer.body}</p>
              <p class="layers__repos">
                {layer.repos.map((r) => (
                  <a href={`https://github.com/Iridium-Group/${r}`} rel="noopener noreferrer">
                    {r}
                  </a>
                ))}
              </p>
            </div>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="wisp-title">
    <div class="ir-container">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2 id="wisp-title">Browser networking with Wisp</h2>
        <p>Why a web page needs help to open a plain TCP connection, and how Wisp provides it.</p>
      </div>
      <ArchitectureDiagram />
      <div class="prose wisp-prose">
        <p>
          Browsers do not let pages open raw TCP sockets. They can open WebSockets. Wisp is a small
          protocol that carries many TCP streams over a single WebSocket, so a page can ask a server
          to connect somewhere on its behalf and exchange bytes with that connection.
        </p>
        <p>A Wisp session uses four packet types:</p>
        <dl class="packets">
          <div>
            <dt>CONNECT</dt>
            <dd>Opens a stream to a host and port.</dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt>DATA</dt>
            <dd>Carries bytes in either direction.</dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt>CONTINUE</dt>
            <dd>
              Tells the sender how much more it may send, so one busy stream cannot flood the
              socket.
            </dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt>CLOSE</dt>
            <dd>Ends a stream with a reason code.</dd>
          </div>
        </dl>
        <p>
          In iridium-proxy, the browser side encrypts TLS itself, so the server relays bytes it
          cannot read for HTTPS destinations. The server still decides which destinations are
          allowed: the address policy in iridium-transport runs before every connection.
        </p>
        <p>
          iridium-transport also includes its own Wisp client, written against the protocol
          documentation, so Node programs and tests can talk to any Wisp server through the same
          Transport interface.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="upstream-title">
    <div class="ir-container">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2 id="upstream-title">Upstream work</h2>
        <p>
          The proxy stands on open-source projects by Mercury Workshop. Iridium depends on their
          published packages and is a separate group.
        </p>
      </div>
      <table class="upstream">
        <caption class="ir-visually-hidden">Upstream dependencies and their licenses</caption>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col">Project</th>
            <th scope="col">Used for</th>
            <th scope="col">License</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {upstream.map((u) => (
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">
                <a href={u.url} rel="noopener noreferrer">
                  {u.name}
                </a>
                <code>{u.pkg}</code>
              </th>
              <td>{u.role}</td>
              <td class="upstream__license">{u.license}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <p class="prose license-note">
        Because epoxy-transport is AGPL-3.0-only and wisp-js is LGPL-3.0-or-later, iridium-proxy is
        licensed AGPL-3.0-only. All other Iridium repositories are MIT.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .layers {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    counter-reset: layer;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--ir-border);
  }
  .layers li {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(11rem, 15rem) 1fr;
    gap: 0.75rem 2rem;
    padding-block: 1.5rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--ir-border);
    counter-increment: layer;
  }
  .layers h3 {
    font-size: 1.25rem;
  }
  .layers h3::before {
    content: counter(layer, decimal-leading-zero);
    display: block;
    font-family: var(--ir-font-mono);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    font-weight: 400;
    color: var(--ir-accent-soft);
    margin-bottom: 0.375rem;
  }
  .layers p {
    color: var(--ir-text-muted);
    max-width: 44rem;
  }
  .layers__repos {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.5rem 1.25rem;
    margin-top: 0.75rem;
    font-family: var(--ir-font-mono);
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
  }
  .wisp-prose {
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
  }
  .packets {
    margin: 1rem 0 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--ir-border);
  }
  .packets div {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 7rem 1fr;
    gap: 1rem;
    padding-block: 0.625rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--ir-border);
  }
  .packets dt {
    font-family: var(--ir-font-mono);
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    color: var(--ir-accent-soft);
    padding-top: 0.15rem;
  }
  .packets dd {
    margin: 0;
  }
  .upstream {
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
  }
  .upstream th,
  .upstream td {
    text-align: left;
    vertical-align: top;
    padding: 1rem 1.5rem 1rem 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--ir-border);
  }
  .upstream tbody tr:last-child > * {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--ir-border);
  }
  .upstream thead th {
    font-family: var(--ir-font-mono);
    font-size: 0.6875rem;
    font-weight: 400;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    color: var(--ir-text-muted);
    padding-block: 0.625rem;
  }
  .upstream tbody th {
    font-weight: 500;
  }
  .upstream tbody th code {
    display: block;
    width: fit-content;
    margin-top: 0.375rem;
    font-weight: 400;
    color: var(--ir-text-muted);
  }
  .upstream td {
    color: var(--ir-text-muted);
  }
  .upstream__license {
    font-family: var(--ir-font-mono);
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    white-space: nowrap;
    padding-right: 0;
  }
  .license-note {
    margin-top: 1.25rem;
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
  }
  @media (max-width: 52rem) {
    .layers li {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
  @media (max-width: 40rem) {
    .upstream thead {
      display: none;
    }
    .upstream,
    .upstream tbody,
    .upstream tr,
    .upstream th,
    .upstream td {
      display: block;
    }
    .upstream tr {
      border-top: 1px solid var(--ir-border);
      padding-block: 1rem;
    }
    .upstream th,
    .upstream td,
    .upstream tbody tr:last-child > * {
      border: 0;
      padding: 0.25rem 0;
    }
    .upstream tbody tr:last-child {
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--ir-border);
    }
  }
</style>
